    {
      "id": "3aeef1be-076f-4aaa-aeb4-009dac8d21aa",
      "type": "playlists",
      "attributes": {
        "name": "Label Focus: Warp Records",
        "description": "Warp Records is one of the most influential, innovative and eclectic labels of the past three decades. Since being formed by Steve Beckett, Rob Gordon and the late Rob Mitchel, and releasing its first single - Forgemasters' \"Track With No Name” - in 1989, Warp has primarily been a force at the forefront of the electronic genres, but has repeatedly demonstrated an openness for experiments in other directions. Other early releases included Nightmares On Wax’s \"Dextrous\" and LFO’s eponymous single, all of which helped lay the foundation for what would become one of the most influential labels of the ‘90s and beyond. Warp was particularly important in that decade’s British electronica scene, with artists such as Aphex Twin, Squarepusher and Autechre on the roster. Warp later expanded its musical horizons with great success, signing artists like !!!, Battles, Maximo Park and Grizzly Bear. Warp is no longer synonymous with experimental electronica, IDM and ambient, but just as easily folktronica, post-punk, shoegaze, and straightforward pop and rock. This playlist includes highlights from Warp’s exceptional catalog.",
        "bounded": true,
        "duration": "PT3H20M10S",
        "numberOfItems": 45,
