    {
      "id": "421f3ec4-4513-4161-a62f-7bfa081b67da",
      "type": "playlists",
      "attributes": {
        "name": "The Horrors Essentials",
        "description": "London-based The Horrors started out as a wild garage punk band, gaining notoriety for their frantic live shows. Debut full-length ‘Strange House’ (2007) perfectly captured this incarnation of The Horrors, but the band soon evolved and morphed into something quite different. Critically acclaimed ‘Primary Colors’ (2009) involved elements of goth, shoegaze and post-punk, a path they further explored on ‘Skyer’ (2011) and ‘Luminous’ (2014). The fifth studio album ‘V’ followed in September 2017. (Photo: Rovi)",
