    {
      "id": "936848b9-e95c-4a2d-9fbe-2b4f4ecc0e84",
      "type": "playlists",
      "attributes": {
        "name": "Starflyer 59 Essentials",
        "description": "A mainstay of Tooth and Nail Records and alternative Christian rock since the early '90s, and largely revolving around the songwriting of Jason Martin, the sound of Starflyer 59 began as guitar-driven shoegaze but has gradually evolving over the years through new wave, post-punk, dream pop and indie rock, with frequent comparisons to bands like My Bloody Valentine, The Smiths, The Cure, New Order and The Boo Radleys. While Martin is a devout Christian and thanks \"Our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ\" on every record, the vast majority of Starflyer 59 songs are secular in nature, begging to be heard by all lovers of quality alternative rock. Enjoy this collection of their best work. (Photo: Tooth & Nail/press)",
