    {
      "id": "93d29acb-6686-400b-9eac-b4eb5ddb60e2",
      "type": "playlists",
      "attributes": {
        "name": "Slowdive Essentials",
        "description": "Slowdive ranks as the quintessential shoegaze band from the 1990s indie scene. They come armed with ethereal soundscapes and dreamy harmonies tucked in with pillows of hazy noise, but also always evolving and progressing way beyond this narrowing style. Formed in Reading, UK, in the late 1980s and centered around singers and songwriters Rachel Goswell and Neil Halstead, Slowdive released three influential albums during their relatively short life \nspan: 'Just For a Day' (1991), 'Souvlaki' (1993) and the majestic swan song 'Pygmalion' in 1995, where they leaned more toward abstract song structures and ambient electronica than waves of pop-noise. Goswell and Halstead later moved on to the more stoney and ambient folk outfit Mojave 3, as all the members kept busy in various bands and solo activities over the years. Slowdive reunited in 2014, and in 2017 they are finally ready for their first new album in 22 years. (Photo: Rovi) ",
        "bounded": true,
        "duration": "PT1H20M36S",
        "numberOfItems": 15,
